(PRC-43 — `fork the process` performs fork(2); the trailing `the process`
 is optional and bare `fork` works too.
 Also covers: PRC-44 (0 in the child, the child's PID in the parent),
 PRC-46 (`reap any child process` returns the reaped child's PID) and
 PRC-56 (`the reaped status` yields the raw wait4 status word, undecoded —
 exit code 7 encodes as 1792, which is 7 * 256).
 The probe never PRINTS a pid, only compares them, so the output is
 reproducible.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-43.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the parent got a positive pid
   the reaped pid matched the forked pid
   the raw status word is 1792
   bare fork forked too
   its exit code decodes to 3
)
a number called 'the long form child' is fork the process.
If 'the long form child' is 0 then, Exit 7.
If 'the long form child' is greater than 0 then, print "the parent got a positive pid".
a number called 'the long form reaped' is reap any child process.
If 'the long form reaped' is 'the long form child' then, print "the reaped pid matched the forked pid".
a number called status is the reaped status.
print "the raw status word is {status}".
a number called 'the bare form child' is fork.
If 'the bare form child' is 0 then, Exit 3.
a number called 'the bare form reaped' is reap any child process.
If 'the bare form reaped' is 'the bare form child' then, print "bare fork forked too".
print "its exit code decodes to {the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256}".
